{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk","id":761192,"title":"How common should hedge magic be among kinfolk?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-08T20:47:26-08:00","id":761192,"title":"How common should hedge magic be among kinfolk?","content":"Kinfolk are the life's blood of the Garou nation and make up its core infrastructure in the mortal world. Surely over time the opportunity to acquire and pass on the knowledge of hedge magic has happened, so how common do you think it is among the more liberal tribes for kinfolk to know a measure of spirit summoning, healing, hell fire, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:37:37-08:00","id":761230,"title":"","content":"I'd say that it should be fairly rare. The Uktena are the only Tribe that has actively cultivated such magics among their kin (to the extent that some of the books let Uktena buy them on top of Garou powers). I would say that among the other &quot;liberal&quot; Tribes, they should be at least as rare (if not a bit more so) than hedge magicians that have nothing to do with the Garou. Basically, those Tribes might not have the level of stigma against magic the other Tribes have, but they aren't actually promoting it in a fashion that creates a higher than average number of them compared to the general population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T23:18:09-08:00","id":761263,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, but if the Bone Gnawer kin got a hold of some, I could easily see them passing it on to other kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T23:22:38-08:00","id":761264,"title":"","content":"one thing in the W20 Kinfolk book clean up the kin specific numina... especialy... what was its name the one where you form a time with a form of animal or plant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T23:26:11-08:00","id":761266,"title":"","content":"Spirit Chasing. You find it in unsung hero`s page 58","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T23:47:52-08:00","id":761273,"title":"","content":"I'd say that there's probably a greater percentage of sorcerers among the kinfolk than there is among the general human population, just because at least some of them are raised in a culture where magic and the spirit world is objectively known to exist. Definitely among the Uktena they'd probably be even relatively common, maybe as much as one or more per kin community. Some Garou might not want their kin practicing magic or having any real power though, especially in the wake of the Sam Haight incident - clear proof for the conservative side that kin knowing rites and genuine occult lore is a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T00:27:18-08:00","id":761286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761263#post761263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, but if the Bone Gnawer kin got a hold of some, I could easily see them passing it on to other kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>That implies hedge magic is something you can pass around with a short instruction manual. Hedge magic is supposed to require a certain amount of innate talent, combined with intense and long lasting training. Many traditions of it aren't inherently cheap either. Just like going to school, there's the time invested in training itself, but supplies as well.<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem like the Gnawers or their kin would waste time on. Why spend ten years learning how to make potions that cost ~$100 to make instead of learning how to be good at scamming the medical system instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T00:54:56-08:00","id":761298,"title":"","content":"I`m with Random Interrupt here.<br /> Kinfolk know, that there is more than the regular consensus around. Most Garou foster a more spiritual approch to live in their kinfolk, and I\u00b4ve read many a tale (for example in the book of auspices), where Theurges and Spirits activly interacted with kinfolk. In one of these storys, one theurge even offered to teach one disgrunted Kin to be a shaman, so she would understand why their beastly cousins do what they do, and help her comunity in the process.<br /> <br /> To sum it up, Kinfolk has basic knowledge about there being some supernatural things out there, and as such wont dismiss mystic lore outright, when they see it.<br /> <br /> As for the inate talent, well they are part spirit. Less so than real garou, but enough to be special. The very principle of being Kinfolk could be interpreted of them having a glimmer of spirit left in them. Pure breed, wich influences their chances of breeding true, could be seen as an indicator of how close they still are to the spirits, just as it represents in a garou how close to the ideal of their breeds-totem their bloodline is.<br /> (This would also explain, why matings of two garou allway breed true (although as metis), since there is such a concentration of spirit-heritage in their blood.)<br /> With spirits being inately magical creatures, I would argue, that their descendens have at least a higher then average talent for magic. Even for so distant cousins as Kin, I would go so far as to say, that most if not all have the potential of shamanic magic in their veins.<br /> <br /> So we have exposure and inate talent.<br /> <br /> All thats left is opportunity and teaching. This is the crux, whether or not a Kin is going to be magially active in my book. As with any other hedge-magican, magic has to be tought to them.<br /> Here it will greatly depend on the sept and the local customs, wether or not the kin gets the opportunity to get a teacher.<br /> Some may hold their kin down, not trusting them with such power.<br /> However, at least in my oppinion, there are many Kin who would have the opportunity to learn. In many breed-books we see kin participate in gatherings and even rites of the garou.<br /> They can certanly gleam at least something from that.<br /> To top it of, Kin who live in close proximity to the cearn have to know how to not anger the local spirits, and to placate them if they do. For that they have to get the help of an Theurge, and I think most of them would at least give their kin guidelines on how to behave around spirits, than risk being called every other monday to clean up the next begrudged spirit ally.<br /> Book of auspices even states outright an example of a Theurge teaching legit shamanism to a Kin, so it can understand why the spirits had orderd a particular thing.<br /> And this was a bitter, angry kin, not someone who had worked to earn their trust, just the other way around.<br /> <br /> All in all we have people with the knowledge, that magic and mystical things exist, a lot of magic in their bloodline and at least the opportunity to glance at real magic and figure the basics out for themselves.<br /> I\u00b4d say, that hedge-magicans should not be too uncommon amongst Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6112,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","user":"Seki","date":". 11-09-2015, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T04:32:39-08:00","id":761365,"title":"","content":"Hedge Magic is one of the worst explained aspects of the whole cWoD. Everyone can learn it, basically, no inherited ability or mystical transformation required, just experience. So, why don't vampires, mages or werewolves or changelings learn it all the time ?<br /> Sure, it is expensive in XP, but more versatile than most garou gifts, complementary to disciplines, paradox free and not banality dependant. That not just anyone uses it all the time is simply justified by the fact that the WoD is a bit like a gothic punk version of reality and therefore not everyone can be a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Stemming from this Setting statement sorcerers amongst kinfolk would be slightly higher than the average human population, but only slightly. If the kinfolk in and by itself would be a secret sorcerer cult the whole garou/kin-dynamic would be different. So, if the Setting is to be preserved than the number of sorcerers should be pretty low.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T04:45:23-08:00","id":761370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761298#post761298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I`m with Random Interrupt here.<br /> Kinfolk know, that there is more than the regular consensus around. Most Garou foster a more spiritual approch to live in their kinfolk, and I\u00b4ve read many a tale (for example in the book of auspices), where Theurges and Spirits activly interacted with kinfolk. In one of these storys, one theurge even offered to teach one disgrunted Kin to be a shaman, so she would understand why their beastly cousins do what they do, and help her comunity in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is with this, they don't need Sorcery at all to accomplish this. Kinfolk can be taught any gift that doesn't require Rage or Gnosis (Except for those that have Gnosis, then they can learn those gifts as well). To be a shamen in Werewolf terms, all a kinfolk would require is Rite of Summoning and Spirit Speech (no cost, no roll, permanent effect, perfect gift for a kinfolk). So, It becomes the same reason why most Garou don't feel the need to learn Sorcery, when you have access to Gifts and Rites, why would you need to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:30:30-08:00","id":761432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761370#post761370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is with this, they don't need Sorcery at all to accomplish this. Kinfolk can be taught any gift that doesn't require Rage or Gnosis (Except for those that have Gnosis, then they can learn those gifts as well). To be a shamen in Werewolf terms, all a kinfolk would require is Rite of Summoning and Spirit Speech (no cost, no roll, permanent effect, perfect gift for a kinfolk). So, It becomes the same reason why most Garou don't feel the need to learn Sorcery, when you have access to Gifts and Rites, why would you need to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IIRC (and feel free to correct me if this has changed since Revised), kinfolk can learn rites but can't actually perform them and expect to have anything magical happen unless they have the Gnosis merit. Without Gnosis they're not beneficiaries in the Great Pact and so the spirits don't have to listen to them. A kin with Gnosis is absolutely better off just learning Spirit Speech and a few rites. Those without really only have sorcery to go to if they want any mojo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:02:04-08:00","id":761447,"title":"","content":"It is said, that a Kin will learn one, maybe two level one gifts in it's lifetime. Compared to hedge magic, spending 15 to 25 experience points on a gift is a pretty bad deal. The cost and the statement about the number of gifts a kin person will learn underline that these are extremely rare.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk can learn and teach rites, but never perform them. The Gnosis merit doesn't change that. Garou rites can be used as focus for true magick or hedge magic, but besides that, can never be performed by a kin person. Not written in the books, but a kinain or changeling could use a garou rite as bunk, I'd guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T08:09:53-08:00","id":761514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761365#post761365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge Magic is one of the worst explained aspects of the whole cWoD. Everyone can learn it, basically, no inherited ability or mystical transformation required, just experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit of an (under? over?)-statement. Both original Sorcerer and Revised talk about how rare sorcerers are (though, when linked with Mage references, more common than mages); it *does* take more than &quot;just experience&quot; to become one -- it takes dedication, often a natural knack/innate talent for it (though not in the same context as for a True Mage), and years of practice. And *plenty* of sorcerers go through a &quot;mystical transformation&quot; -- especially most of the Bata'a, the Malabob, the Fenian (speaking of kinfolk) and some others -- when becoming sorcerers and/or when advancing their powers. It's not usually as dramatic as for a mage, true, and certainly not the same thing as becoming a vampire or late-blooming into the First Change, but neither should it be underestimated for quite a number of sorcerers in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761365#post761365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stemming from this Setting statement sorcerers amongst kinfolk would be slightly higher than the average human population, but only slightly. If the kinfolk in and by itself would be a secret sorcerer cult the whole garou/kin-dynamic would be different. So, if the Setting is to be preserved than the number of sorcerers should be pretty low.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more on-point correct. There would be, proportionally, more kinfolk who had a modicum of sorcerous ability/practice (possibly coupled with a Gift or two, over time) than would occur in the broader population (especially when kinfolk only number in so many thousands in any given tribe, overall, and the world is populated by 7+billion people), but generally if there are (for simple math's sake) 100,000 kinfolk, then only a couple/few hundred of them would be sorcerers, and even then only have a handful of dots (with the rarer &quot;real Sorcerers(tm)&quot; -- those who would be full-fledged PCs with experience -- being only a fraction of those). That's still much, much higher than found in the broader population, but a still very uncommon thing proportionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T08:19:06-08:00","id":761521,"title":"","content":"Oh a question? Think the more Fascist tribes (Like shadow lords and Silver Fangs or Fianna?) Are more likely to discourage kinfolk from learning numina... I could see wanting a kinfolk to know Alchemy or Divination.. hmmmn oh what about Psychic Numina??<br /> <br /> Those just appear randomly rather then through study...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-09-2015, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T09:14:45-08:00","id":761543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761365#post761365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge Magic is one of the worst explained aspects of the whole cWoD. Everyone can learn it, basically, no inherited ability or mystical transformation required, just experience. So, why don't vampires, mages or werewolves or changelings learn it all the time ?<br /> Sure, it is expensive in XP, but more versatile than most garou gifts, complementary to disciplines, paradox free and not banality dependant. That not just anyone uses it all the time is simply justified by the fact that the WoD is a bit like a gothic punk version of reality and therefore not everyone can be a sorcerer.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I distinctly remember a Silent Strider talking about human magic that Garou could learn and saying that spending the time learning it rather than the power of the spirits would be spitting in the faces of the spirits who offer their power to the Garou. Or at least it was in one of the Tribe Books. Vampires are stagnant, and probably find branching out into non-clan discipline territory uncomfortable enough as it is, much less something far more dynamic that mortal magic; and as for the rest, who knows,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 11-09-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:38:34-08:00","id":761825,"title":"","content":"Most responses have covered the basics, so I'll just add that 'Kin to who?'<br /> <br /> I'd think the the Get of Fenris or Wendigo probably have very few, while the Uktena, Bubasti , and Mokole actively promote it. Glasswalkers probably don't realize they do, because to them, it's 'computers' and 'science'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T17:16:25-08:00","id":761849,"title":"","content":"I kind of see hedge magic as being relatively common among the kinfolk. Common in that it isn't seen as being extremely bizarre, though hedge magic practitioners are still a relatively small minority. I wouldn't think that it would be seen as some entirely different sort of power from what werewolves use, but rather another way of connecting to the spirit world. I think that the kinfolk should still be a part of the Garou culture and have some limited knowledge of the spirit world and even access to supernatural powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T18:18:28-08:00","id":761897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761286#post761286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge magic is supposed to require a certain amount of innate talent, combined with intense and long lasting training. Many traditions of it aren't inherently cheap either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely. The amount of justification to have such knowledge is often overlooked because mechanics-wise, you just buy it with XP. In &quot;reality&quot; though, you have to devoted your life to mastering such esoteric knowledge. Any form of magic is a kind of spiritual discipline, but that doesn't show up when it comes to acquiring it in game.<br /> <br /> I would not be surprised if at various times, a secret lodge among the kinfolk arose that had knowledge of hedge magic. However, the Garou are jealous of their status as Gaia's defenders, and if they find out about it - which they eventually will - things will not turn out well for those kinfolk hedge wizards.<br /> <br /> Players often have a &quot;we're in this all together&quot; so it's great for the Garou if their kinfolk are mages, hedge wizards, or whatever. This is a very naive view of how protective of their turf people are, and how much infighting occurs within organizations.<br /> <br /> Even if some kinfolk only had access to Ephemera - which is justifiable based on the kinfolk base of knowledge - I don't think the Garou would be supportive of it. The kinfolk are usurping the role of the Garou and being uppity. If such things exist, it's probably very limited - with specific paths being available within specific sects/traditions of specific tribes, and being overseen/approved by elder Garou to make sure such magic if done &quot;properly&quot; and controlled.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T18:49:21-08:00","id":761924,"title":"","content":"Most Garou wouldn't, but what about CoG or Bone Gnawers? The latter seems suitably humble to not hold back their family if one of them has the means to develop a talent for magic.<br /> <br /> Edit: Although, admittedly, we're talking about a talent that can take years to develop to a meaningful level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 11-09-2015, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T23:20:56-08:00","id":762027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761924#post761924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Garou wouldn't, but what about CoG or Bone Gnawers? The latter seems suitably humble to not hold back their family if one of them has the means to develop a talent for magic.<br /> <br /> Edit: Although, admittedly, we're talking about a talent that can take years to develop to a meaningful level.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the Kinfolk book put CoG as pretty supportive of Kin with 'odd' talents. (Something that they, weirdly enough, had in common with Shadow Lords. The whole 'any tool to an end' thing.)<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers probably wouldn't care either way. They wouldn't reject any useful ability, but at the same time, the amount of time and energy that would go into most forms of magic probably wouldn't be appreciated.<br /> <br /> Edit: That said, that really mainly applies to the 'study and work' methods. The 'idiot savant', crazy lady that does weird things would fit right in. But again, it might not even be seen as 'magic' by the Bone Gnawers. \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5818,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","user":"EvilTyger","date":". 11-10-2015, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T23:31:08-08:00","id":762033,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"color:#fff\">\u21b5</span></span> Is there something specific you are after or interested in? Aiming at a specific concept or idea?<br /> <br /> I've long since lost them, but at one point I had a brief writeup for a Society based on the modern descendants of the Danislavs (long ago having 'bred out' the whole Revnant thing), a Formori Brotherhood that liked to blame the Followers of Set for their shenanigans, and a traveling troupe of Bastet Kin entertainers (that used slight of hand and other deceptions as much as powers). \u200b<br /> <br /> I also know one player/ST that (before Sorcerer was released) took the Gypsy book and completely rehashed the 'lupine family' into Shadow Lord kin with some minor ties to the Silent Striders.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5818,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","user":"EvilTyger","date":". 11-10-2015, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T23:42:24-08:00","id":762041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761543#post761543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Vampires are stagnant, and probably find branching out into non-clan discipline territory uncomfortable enough as it is, much less something far more dynamic that mortal magic[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires can't learn/use mortal hedge magic any more than they can use True Magic(k) -- it's cited in several different books (vampire and mage) that as undead beings they don't have the connection to the world that a living being does, so the only route for them is blood magic (paths and disciplines). So they never come up for cross comparisons in that respect, regardless...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T00:59:43-08:00","id":762072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=762041#post762041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can't learn/use mortal hedge magic any more than they can use True Magic(k) -- it's cited in several different books (vampire and mage) that as undead beings they don't have the connection to the world that a living being does, so the only route for them is blood magic (paths and disciplines). So they never come up for cross comparisons in that respect, regardless...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> That is not entirely correct. Vampires cannot use True Magic anymore, but the differences between mortal hedge Magic and vampiric blood Magic is largely academic. There is not a unified hedge magic, but many different variants, blood magic is one of the many shades found.<br /> Do not look too much to Revised ed. fluff. Revised was the try to stuff a) personal horror, b) personal horror and c) Do not play WoD without only focusing on personal horror down the players throats.We laughed long and hard at the rules on Mages using Vampiric Vitae in &quot;Blood Treachery&quot;. They were totally over the top, full of fear of power gamers and trying to enforce personal horror. A ST not able to simply use the potentail blood bond the Mage might walk into to full effect does not derserve to ST. That is the main failure of Revised. Rulewise it was the best version until V20, but the authors tried to force a single type of play on the players and several metaplot decisions are best left uncommented. There is a reason why several retcons are found in V20 and W20 I think too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T01:11:57-08:00","id":762076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=762072#post762072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> That is not entirely correct. Vampires cannot use True Magic anymore, but the differences between mortal hedge Magic and vampiric blood Magic is largely academic. There is not a unified hedge magic, but many different variants, blood magic is one of the many shades found.<br /> Do not look too much to Revised ed. fluff. Revised was the try to stuff a) personal horror, b) personal horror and c) Do not play WoD without only focusing on personal horror down the players throats.We laughed long and hard at the rules on Mages using Vampiric Vitae in &quot;Blood Treachery&quot;. They were totally over the top, full of fear of power gamers and trying to enforce personal horror. A ST not able to simply use the potentail blood bond the Mage might walk into to full effect does not derserve to ST. That is the main failure of Revised. Rulewise it was the best version until V20, but the authors tried to force a single type of play on the players and several metaplot decisions are best left uncommented. There is a reason why several retcons are found in V20 and W20 I think too.</div> </div> </div> </div>TL;DR your wrong but I can't site sources. That's pretty much what I got out of your post.<br /> <br /> Vampires can't learn hedge magic any more then ghouls can learn thaumaturgy....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 11-10-2015, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T01:37:07-08:00","id":762088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=762076#post762076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> TL;DR your wrong but I can't site sources. That's pretty much what I got out of your post.<br /> <br /> Vampires can't learn hedge magic any more then ghouls can learn thaumaturgy....</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but the reason you cannot cite sources is because I am right. Hedge magic is not unified, the various &quot;Traditions&quot; differ how and what quintessence pool they tap for their magic. Thaumaturgy is one of the many variants.<br /> By the way, Ghouls can learn Thau. It is just that outside the Tremere and Tzimisce (Kolduns) Clans it is very rarely done, due to either lacking knowledge or lacking the blood they need to start learning. It is in the V20 rules as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","user":"G\u00fcnther","date":". 11-10-2015, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T01:40:56-08:00","id":762091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=762072#post762072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> That is not entirely correct. Vampires cannot use True Magic anymore, but the differences between mortal hedge Magic and vampiric blood Magic is largely academic. There is not a unified hedge magic, but many different variants, blood magic is one of the many shades found.<br /> Do not look too much to Revised ed. fluff. Revised was the try to stuff a) personal horror, b) personal horror and c) Do not play WoD without only focusing on personal horror down the players throats.We laughed long and hard at the rules on Mages using Vampiric Vitae in &quot;Blood Treachery&quot;. They were totally over the top, full of fear of power gamers and trying to enforce personal horror. A ST not able to simply use the potentail blood bond the Mage might walk into to full effect does not derserve to ST. That is the main failure of Revised. Rulewise it was the best version until V20, but the authors tried to force a single type of play on the players and several metaplot decisions are best left uncommented. There is a reason why several retcons are found in V20 and W20 I think too.</div> </div> </div> </div>My post was *essentially* correct; that is, vampires *can't* use mortal hedge-magic (sans the Golden Rule, of course, but that should go without saying), and that's been the case since 1st Edition. Vampires can <i>bastardize</i> hedge magic via adapting their own blood magic/vitae to &quot;make shit work&quot;, but that is metaphysically a very different thing in the broader picture. Vampires lose their connection to the living forces of the world, and as a result lose the ability to work both True Magic(k) and mortal hedge magic (this was covered in several different books pre-Revised, then stressed again in Revised, particularly in Sorcerer, which was of course all about hedge magic). It is why vampiric Thaumaturgy (by whatever name) is usually more potent (generally a given dot rating in Thaumaturgy/a Path has more &quot;oomph&quot; than a Sorcerer's Paths do) but often less flexible (Sorcerer paths -- and some of their Psychic Numina, where overlapping -- have more flexibility/facet-use than the Paths of Blood Magic that vampires can practice). Also, don't confuse/conflate the narrative aspect that some sorcerers may use animal sacrifice/blood, or their own blood, as a component of a given spell/ritual as that then being &quot;blood magic&quot; -- <i>it isn't</i>. The Blood Magic that vampires practice is metaphysically quite different from what mortal hedge wizards do; sometimes the results may be nigh-identical, true, but the specific underlying *how*/*why* is very, very different, and this shouldn't be overlooked as it in turn is what leads to a number of misunderstandings about the metaphysics involved....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  spelling 11-10-2015, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T01:50:07-08:00","id":762096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=762076#post762076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> TL;DR your wrong but I can't site sources. That's pretty much what I got out of your post.<br /> <br /> Vampires can't learn hedge magic any more then ghouls can learn thaumaturgy....</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm... *yeah* -- I gotta go with Gunther on this one: ghouls *can* learn Thaumaturgy, it just is rare for them to do so as very few vampires share that kind of knowledge with &quot;the help&quot;, and it also would require the vampire-regnant in question to feed his ghoul <i>very</i> regularly... something even fewer vampires are inclined to do. The only long-standing exceptions are the Rafastio witch-ghouls of the Black Hand, who had Thaumaturgy as an in-&quot;clan&quot; discipline (along with Animalism and Auspex); however, they were also Revenants, and therefore capable of maintaining their own, albeit limited, vitae for powering their spells/rituals (and most STs --including myself-- that I knew Golden Ruled that they could raise their Thaumaturgy to 5 regardless the standard blood-limits that ghouls usually operate under -- this better reflected the cross-melding of vampiric-vitae with mortal hedge magic... one of the only cases where this might occur, per my further up posts...). But anywho...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T02:04:38-08:00","id":762106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=762091#post762091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My post was *essentially* correct; that is, vampires *can't* use mortal hedge-magic (sans the Golden Rule, of course, but that should go without saying), and that's been the case since 1st Edition. Vampires can <i>bastardize</i> hedge magic via adapting their own blood magic/vitae...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> In the older editions how complete the loss of connections to the mortal world was and how it affected Vamp Hedge Magic was handled variably. Only Revised tried to push personal horror and divide the WoD systems at all costs. There are many reasons why I consider Revised to be 80% manure, 10% ok, 10% good. In older books there are strong hints that Thaumaturgy is not the nicest version of hedge magic, but just a different variant of all the other hedge magic traditions out there, which makes more sense, especially since despite the Vamps being supernatural they are part of the natural WoD ecology, an &quot;unnatural&quot; balance of nature. But keeping it like that would have prevented new money-making books and dividing the settings more..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T03:46:54-08:00","id":762164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761543#post761543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distinctly remember a Silent Strider talking about human magic that Garou could learn and saying that spending the time learning it rather than the power of the spirits would be spitting in the faces of the spirits who offer their power to the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this, if one would learn hedge magic today. But the statement is flawed in too regards<br /> 1. If garou would have since ever occasionally learned hedge magic to have more versatile powers gifts can supply the spirits would have no reason to be pissed if garou did so - for it would be an established practice.<br /> 2. And most importantly, hedge magic is just a rules construct. Within the Setting a sorcerer has still to use specific styles or traditions and garou would go the shamanic or druidic way. So, their hedge magic would, just like their garou rites, work in accordance with the spirits. It's not like garou would usually go hermetic, voodoo or some other non-spirit style to do hedge magic. From a mages standpoint gifts and disciplines and hedge magic is all linear magic. So shamanic based hedge magic would just be another way to explain gifts.<br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to vampires the older sorcerer book had a conversion of hedge magic to disciplines and arcanoi. So, if a sorcerer became a malkavian, he might still have thauma from the get go and possibly able to raise his traits or learn new rituals - converting them from non-vitae based sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 11-10-2015, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:20:32-08:00","id":762446,"title":"","content":"Hey guys?<br /> <br /> This is a WtA thread. How much distinction you want between vampire Blood Sorcery, and mortal Hedge Magic, is irrelevant to how many kinfolk know Hedge Magic.<br /> <br /> As well... lets try to get away from arguing about editions. Fanning the flames of an edition war will do... nothing good for the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:29:17-08:00","id":762449,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea of Kinfolk traditions learning Sorcery, being taught as a method of passing down legacies of power among kinfolk. For instance old Italian members of the Tribe that is now the Glasswalkers were Alchemists and cultivating kinfolk usefulness was natural for the tribe so why not teach them alchemy.<br /> <br /> Yes Garou are often very conservative, and will also take pride in not directly pressing their family into the endless war, but still some communities have no choice but to call the kinfolk to aid them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T13:22:13-08:00","id":762554,"title":"","content":"That's how I see it. I figure that a Garou's special relationship to everything under Gaia would strongly discourage them from &quot;distractions&quot; but that some septs would want kinfolk who could at least provide a last line of defense for the Sept's kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:14:34-08:00","id":762588,"title":"","content":"The question though, is why would the Garou go outside of their usual arenas of power for having some &quot;beefier&quot; kinfolk? There's lots of stuff in the books for making special kinfolk that can do things beyond the baseline abilities. I'm pretty sure the Garou would much rather try to encourage kinfolk with a connection to Gaia via Gnosis rather than encouraging human-magics.<br /> <br /> The books also establish that the Garou are capable of doing things like making Talens and Fetishes that any kinfolk can use.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm totally on board with there being some magical skills among the kinfolk. That's always been part of things. It just seems like there's a tendency to put our external idea of what would be practical/too good to pass up, over what the Garou would actually know and accept from their perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:23:53-08:00","id":762598,"title":"","content":"Teaching kinfolk about gaia, about gifts, about the enemy and about magic is often justified with the ability of the kin to help in the war or defend sept, caern or themselves. But doesn't it make garou weak to share their burdens. Doesn't it make them dishonourable to distribute their holy burden to others, not born true?<br /> <br /> I can see garou tolerating their kin learning magic, but not to take on their roles. The garou are the chosen ones and their care for their kin. While certainly some kin find their true born relatives captivating and want to protect them and dedicate their lives to do so, garou still wouldn't and shouldn't encourage them to enter or even be backup in their duties.<br /> <br /> So, wise women mumbling divinations, or barkeeper-types handing out some enchanted meat to the cliath pack leaving for a mission is probably okay, but fire ball throwing sentries or guardians with magical blades not so much.<br /> <br /> But in any case it should be rare. Sorcery requires a type of dedication and willpower not every one can simply pick up. Just like most people could train to be an Olympia level athlete, but most do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T19:24:02-08:00","id":762763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=762106#post762106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> In the older editions how complete the loss of connections to the mortal world was and how it affected Vamp Hedge Magic was handled variably. Only Revised tried to push personal horror and divide the WoD systems at all costs. There are many reasons why I consider Revised to be 80% manure, 10% ok, 10% good. In older books there are strong hints that Thaumaturgy is not the nicest version of hedge magic, but just a different variant of all the other hedge magic traditions out there, which makes more sense, especially since despite the Vamps being supernatural they are part of the natural WoD ecology, an &quot;unnatural&quot; balance of nature. But keeping it like that would have prevented new money-making books and dividing the settings more..<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing of what I posted invalidates that. Vampiric Thaumaturgy is a *bastardization* of existing, mortal Hedge Magic. That is, if you put a given Tremere (particularly one from several centuries ago) next to a Hermetic, who had a certain Verbena/Old Faith-subset witch next to him, and a couple variant Aeon sorcerers sitting over in the corner, the average observer would think that each of them were performing essentially the same ritual/spell/what-have-you that specifically does &quot;X&quot; (as those specific characters I'm citing have several points of ritual overlap with each other in several regards). However, metaphysically, each of them would merely have similar trappings about them but would otherwise being accomplishing their mojo in *very* different ways: The Hermetic and the witch may use the same arcane symbols, Latin, and herbs that the Tremere is, but the first is harnessing power through his [Avatar] and (likely) channeling power from the High Umbra to accomplish &quot;X&quot;, while the second is calling upon natural elemental forces (and possibly no spiritual entreatment at all), while the third is simply using the arcane symbols around him to channel the innate power of his undead vitae to manifest the same mystical effect. The two Aeon sorcerers in the corner are harnessing the power of remaining mythic threads that &quot;permit&quot; &quot;X&quot; to still occur in the world, but this is through no direct innate power of their own, inherently, unlike with the Tremere (whose power solely comes from within), the Hermetic (who god-shard empowers him while the Umbrood he entreats gives his magic purpose and meaning), and the witch (whose mojo actually combines facets of raw elements coupled with a few bits linked to how the others all do their thing... only a little different).<br /> <br /> Not only are each of those characters doing things differently on one level, they are also doing it differently on a different metaphysical level (the two Mages via True Magick, the two Sorcerers via the mortal Hedge Magic, and the Tremere via his vitae descending down from Caine/Lilith). While that means nothing to Joe Schmoe, personally, it makes a big difference mystically: the Mages can potentially pull off a bigger &quot;showing&quot; of mojo than the others, but at the risk of Paradox due to operating on a level of True, Dynamic Magick; the Sorcerers' ritual may or may not work, depending on how &quot;impossible&quot; the end result is (Hedge Magic will outright fail in the Modern Times if it in too-direct opposition to Reality(tm), but do so without risk of Paradox; the Tremere, on the other hand, can have his mojo work regardless of the viewer and/or most of the broader Reality(tm), but at the cost of flexibility of power as well as having &quot;paradox&quot; manifest in a different manner for him (vampiric vulnerability to sunlight, etc., as translated into Mage).<br /> <br /> Just as only the very rarest of Mages can ever possess any numina/static hedge-powers, vampires can't utilize the mortal hedge magic that *living* beings can access (as indicated by some were-cats and Uktena being practitioners of Hedge Magic, in addition to the broader human sorcerers) any more than they can access True Magick; they can, however, adapt their own inherent essences to mimic/bastardize &quot;X&quot; via their vitae, but as indicated this is a separate metaphysical process with marked strengths and limitations when compared to the other witchy-pooh being bandied about.<br /> <br /> A very important metaphysical distinction that should *not* be overlooked....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T19:37:14-08:00","id":762768,"title":"","content":"Anywho...<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Some tribes -- and even more on point/specifically, some packs -- would be more pre-disposed to having kinfolk learn Gifts/Hedge Magic than others, so it really just depends. It's easy enough to see certain Shadowlords finding value in a given kinfolk who has the innate talent/pre-disposition for a Gift or two, or who developed a Path or three of Hedge magic, to be of great use in plotting against others (both trans-and-inter-tribal, as well as with outsiders in general), while most other 'lords would see it as a threat/liability. Plenty of Black Furies would be perfectly fine with their &quot;less-blessed&quot; sisters developing Hedge Magic -- this is most especially true with the Greek Furies who still maintain ties with their Amazon sisters who themselves practice both True and Hedge Magic(k). The average Get wouldn't get caught dead having his kinfolk get &quot;that uppity&quot;, while the Red Talons would, by-and-large, see the entire system of monkey-magic undone altogether.<br /> <br /> So it really just depends.<br /> <br /> As stated by myself and some others earlier, however, it *should* still be an uncommon/rare thing -- more common compared to the broader human population, certainly, but still a matter of only a few hundred, at the very most, out of a given 100,000 (and even then, a large part of that represents individuals who simply have a Gift or two and maybe a handful of dots in one or two Paths -- true, full-on Sorcerers should be counted in the scores at that point).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T06:35:01-08:00","id":763061,"title":"","content":"Depend also of the Path of Hedge magic of course. Even Get of Fenris would see nothing wrong with a kinfolk runecaster.or healer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:03:21-08:00","id":763156,"title":"","content":"That's not really how the books portray it. The books generally show that the Garou as a whole (and the more traditional Tribes like the Fenrir especially) consider all human magics a form of humans stepping out of their place and contributing to the world being out of balance. Especially as few Garou would know the difference (or necessarily care) about all the different kinds of magic out there.<br /> <br /> The basic hardline position is that humans, including kinfolk, are not supposed to have these powers. How individual magic users are dealt with is a matter of if the Garou are going to tolerate this breach in their world view (keeping in mind Garou tolerate lots of violations of how they say things should be done all the time). The Fenrir couldn't give a damn if your practices look like traditional practices of their cultural background if they also think you're forcing spirits to do you bidding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T13:43:54-08:00","id":763410,"title":"","content":"Be careful to not have the NPCs reading the character sheets. They aren't going to automatically know that a character is using 'Path X'. Under most faith and shamanistic paradigms, the practitioner has no power at all, they have to ask nicely. Tach based paradigms aren't about power directly, but knowledge.<br /> <br /> The mechanics being the same doesn't mean all magic = Hermetic from an in character perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:05:05-08:00","id":763629,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Garou are dicks about magic. To them the Dreamspeakers and the Technocrats are almost the same thing.<br /> They do have a point, considering what Mages are in Werewolf cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:50:44-08:00","id":763654,"title":"","content":"Actually, the Wendigo are surprisingly okay about human shamans as long as they are Native Americans. At least as I remember. I suspect they are nostalgic about even old foes in this age of strip malls and techno sorcery and are open to working with shamans who come from their people and work under their paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T19:21:05-08:00","id":763671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=763629#post763629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Garou are dicks about magic. To them the Dreamspeakers and the Technocrats are almost the same thing.<br /> They do have a point, considering what Mages are in Werewolf cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Dream-speaker' and 'Technocrat' are both political bodies. Being part of an MtA political body is not required in order to work magic.<br /> <br /> If a Kinfolk carefully collects a batch of herbs and makes a poultice, a player will know the difference between high level skills like medicine and herbalism, or low level paths like Healing or Binding. <br /> <br /> Even if it's something more obvious, such abilities don't manifest overnight. Chances are that the Garou around them wouldn't notice, due to familiarity.<br /> <br /> Of course, if they start wiggling their fingers, chanting in backwards Latin, and fireballs fall from the sky, there's going to be problems. But that is hardly the bulk of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T19:40:31-08:00","id":763683,"title":"","content":"I think it is worth noting that Gifts like Sense the Unnatural, Scent of the True Form, and Sense Magic do allow the Garou to tell the difference (though not easily) between high levels of mundane herbalism, and the Path of Alchemy and/or Healing. Those Gifts do not differentiate based on &quot;paradigm&quot; and sense the Hermetic, the Technocrat, and the Shaman the same way. Which means they're more disposed to not trust human shamans, because their Gifts for sensing magic use ping the same as a human wizard. &quot;Garou are dicks about magic&quot; is actually backed up by the mechanics making them very bad at detecting the differences you're talking about, and better and just noting human magic in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T02:18:15-08:00","id":763878,"title":"","content":"If a Garou relies only upon what pings their senses and doesn't try to develop any deeper understanding once they know something's pinging, of course they're going to act like complete idiots and treat everyone the same way. But their gifts aren't meant to be used as the beginning <i>and</i> the end of their investigations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-12-2015, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T13:24:06-08:00","id":764340,"title":"","content":"So... how does a Garou investigate the difference between a Hermetic spirit focused magician (regardless of mechanics), and a shaman, that allows them to actually draw a distinction between, &quot;this is a true shaman that honors Gaia and operates according to her ways,&quot; and, &quot;this is someone that has been deluded by human magical powers to thinking that's what they're doing, but they're actually being Name Breakers just like wizards.&quot;<br /> <br /> They have powers that ignore magical style and just detect magic use. They can investigate, but most of their powers that try to defeat lies work against malicious lying, rather than simply believing something factually incorrect. They, essentially, have extremely limited ability (if any) to figure out anything more than, &quot;this human works a form of magic, and is trying to do right by the spirits.&quot;<br /> <br /> But they're culturally taught not to trust humanity, let alone human magic. Even if they're going to be nicer to the shaman than the wizard, they're still stuck in a default position of having little way to prove the position of, &quot;any unsupervised human magic is too dangerous to allow,&quot; incorrect, and thus forced to either press-gang shamans and keep a close eye on them, or tell them to stop or else, rather than just killing them like they might a Hermetic or Technocrat stepping where they shouldn't have.<br /> <br /> Also, frankly, WtA is full of the Garou being idiots by trusting their gut instincts instead of developing deeper understandings. The Garou are pretty much stuck in an ageless cycle of not thinking things through well enough before acting, and their actions ending up being massively bad choices in hindsight. WtA is supposed to be a game where the pressure to act regularly beats the need to develop deep understanding of issues. The Garou don't have time to spend months determining the fate of each human magic user they meet. They have a Wyrm to defeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T15:47:53-08:00","id":764459,"title":"","content":"Also, keep in mind that mages are rare. Most Garou will never actually meet a Mage, and they are more likely to meet Mages who aggressivley seek out their Caerns then peaceful ones that want to drink beer with them. It's hard to build a relationship when the majority of your interactions are painted by the depravity of one side and the zeal of the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T16:42:02-08:00","id":764509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764340#post764340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, frankly, WtA is full of the Garou being idiots by trusting their gut instincts instead of developing deeper understandings. The Garou are pretty much stuck in an ageless cycle of not thinking things through well enough before acting, and their actions ending up being massively bad choices in hindsight. WtA is supposed to be a game where the pressure to act regularly beats the need to develop deep understanding of issues. The Garou don't have time to spend months determining the fate of each human magic user they meet. They have a Wyrm to defeat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not entirely true. One of the things about Apocalypse is trying not to repeat the mistakes of the past.<br /> <br /> As to how they might investigate rather than kill? Well, if they sense kinfolk using magic they might hold back and <i>find out what the hell is going on</i> instead of going on a murder spree over it.<br /> <br /> There's always an excuse for Garou doing the stupidest possible thing, but surely players can rise above that.<br /> <br /> Besides there was a sidebar in WW Rev about sense wyrm not being &quot;detect evil.&quot; This applies to the other sense gifts as well: They aren't an unerring arrow pointed toward &quot;kill this now&quot; they're an information gathering tool.<br /> <br /> But sure if you want to play your werewolves like a pack of idiots slaughtering everything that looks at them sideways, that's your choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T16:42:32-08:00","id":764511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764459#post764459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, keep in mind that mages are rare. Most Garou will never actually meet a Mage, and they are more likely to meet Mages who aggressivley seek out their Caerns then peaceful ones that want to drink beer with them. It's hard to build a relationship when the majority of your interactions are painted by the depravity of one side and the zeal of the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but back up a minute and remember we're talking about kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T16:47:22-08:00","id":764513,"title":"","content":"'Mages don't use magic, they ARE magic' was the phrase in 2nd ed Mage, and scent of True Form still had a dif 9 to detect them. IIRC, questions about them detecting Sorcerers or Psychics always came back as 'depends on the game'. (Would you allow the gift to detect Uktena Path Dancers?)<br /> <br /> That's the most common of those gifts. <br /> <br /> The others are less common, no less difficult, and are as often (if not more often) used by those that would have a more favorable reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:49:13-08:00","id":764571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764340#post764340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... how does a Garou investigate the difference between a Hermetic spirit focused magician (regardless of mechanics), and a shaman, that allows them to actually draw a distinction between, &quot;this is a true shaman that honors Gaia and operates according to her ways,&quot; and, &quot;this is someone that has been deluded by human magical powers to thinking that's what they're doing, but they're actually being Name Breakers just like wizards.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The simplest answer would be to talk to the spirits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T20:17:42-08:00","id":764672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764509#post764509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to how they might investigate rather than kill? Well, if they sense kinfolk using magic they might hold back and <i>find out what the hell is going on</i> instead of going on a murder spree over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did... you read my post? Or just quote a part and ignore the following bit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's always an excuse for Garou doing the stupidest possible thing, but surely players can rise above that. </div> </div> </div>We're not really talking about what iconoclastic PCs might do. We're talking about how common magic users should be among the kinfolk, on a tangent of how much the Garou don't like human magic, even among the kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides there was a sidebar in WW Rev about sense wyrm not being &quot;detect evil.&quot; This applies to the other sense gifts as well: They aren't an unerring arrow pointed toward &quot;kill this now&quot; they're an information gathering tool. </div> </div> </div>Which is nice, but ignoring the point. If a Garou discovers a kinfolk turned vampire using various sensory Gifts, the vast majority of Garou are going to kill the kinfolk-vampire. Not because they're treating Sense Wyrm as dectect evil. But because they consider being a vampire being worse than dead, and once they find out a kin is a vampire they're going to kill it.<br /> <br /> The Garou response to human magic isn't as extreme, but it falls into the same general issue. Finding out a kinfolk is using human magic is already putting that kinfolk into the &quot;shit list&quot; pile. Not because Sense Magic is detect Name Breaker, but because it doesn't take a lot of investigation to say, &quot;Hey what's this magic smell you've got on you? Wait, you're resorting to human magic? WTF!?!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But sure if you want to play your werewolves like a pack of idiots slaughtering everything that looks at them sideways, that's your choice. </div> </div> </div>If you want to derail the thread with silly badwrongfun accusations and snide comments, that's your choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764571#post764571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simplest answer would be to talk to the spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Name breakers can force the spirits to say things... so... now what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T20:50:43-08:00","id":764693,"title":"","content":"I've always bin of the mind that sorcery is more then just &quot;here kid read a book, your a wizard now!&quot;. That the individual was born under a sign, right condition or destined somehow to wield the power.<br /> <br /> Granted some old guy who has studied his whole life might know a dot or two in a path but the real deal was destined for it.<br /> <br /> That said the garou would know at least something was special about the kid, maybe he under go the change later on or he might be able to talk to spirits or she might awaken into a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T21:11:11-08:00","id":764703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764672#post764672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Name breakers can force the spirits to say things... so... now what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for my answer seeming simple. I meant doing research and talking to various spirits and asking around and such. As a Garou, spirits are your kin, and mentors and Gods. A lot can be accomplished with proper chiminage and polite questions.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I also don't think Garou are as rabidly against the entirety of magic use as you seem to be sure they are, so there is that.<br /> <br /> My opinion on the Garou's opinion of magic aside, I don't see a Hermetic (or any Mage really) running around, casting spell after spell to make sure particular Spirits will speak kindly of him should a Garou come around asking. Do I believe that could be accomplished by a dedicated Mage? Sure...mage as a system can do pretty much anything. But (especially from a WtA perspective) no Mage would actually do that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T23:32:12-08:00","id":764746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764693#post764693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said the garou would know at least something was special about the kid, maybe he under go the change later on or he might be able to talk to spirits or she might awaken into a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the edition's specific mechanics (there's a different thread about this) the Garou have ways of knowing (usually) which kids are meant to be Garou and which aren't. So they'd be able to sort children born under various omens and what not into at least &quot;probably Garou meant for something special,&quot; and, &quot;probably kinfolk that's touched in some way.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764703#post764703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant doing research and talking to various spirits and asking around and such. As a Garou, spirits are your kin, and mentors and Gods. A lot can be accomplished with proper chiminage and polite questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can solve all/most/a lot of your problems by asking the spirits nicely, most of WtA doesn't work. The spirits might know a lot, but they aren't meant to be omniscient (at least not the ones that are going to answer requests like this; Gaia isn't going to be happy if you're ringing her up for this sort of thing). There's no guarantee the local spirits have any idea.<br /> <br /> And this still gets into the issue that I've raised that hasn't really been addressed: why the hell are any Garou wasting their time on this? And now wasting the spirits time? A kin magic user is either going to obey the rules the Garou place on them, or the Garou aren't likely to try to parse out all this stuff in favor of doing something more drastic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, I also don't think Garou are as rabidly against the entirety of magic use as you seem to be sure they are, so there is that. </div> </div> </div>I'll quote W20:<br /> <br /> &quot;Many Garou see mages as usurpers of Gaia\u2019s rightful power as creator. They feel that the versatile and powerful magic these witches wield is the birthright of Celestines alone, and yearn to see the vainglorious mages humbled. The fact that some mages have attempted to raid the Garou\u2019s caems for spiritual energy (and drained more than a few in the process) does not improve the werewolves\u2019 attitudes about them.<br /> ...<br /> Mages who attempt flashy or showy effects (especially in public places, where normal people can see them) often suffer mysterious injuries. (They explode, blood spurts from their eyes, their flesh peels off, and some even vanish without a trace.) The Garou consider this just and appropriate: the hand of Mother Gaia (or the Weaver) disciplining her wayward creations.&quot;<br /> <br /> Though that last part only really relevant to dynamic Mages and hedge mages/psychics with specific flaws.<br /> <br /> As to the kin-mage shaman:<br /> <br /> &quot;She is Kinfolk to the Garou, and she helps when she can (or must), but even her blood kinship can\u2019t overcome the distrust many elders feel for her kind. A few extreme Garou believe that human mages who practice shamanic or nature-oriented magic are trying to steal their birthright as Gaia\u2019s chosen by emulating them.<br /> ...<br /> She\u2019s learned the secrets of Voudoun, but she at least gives lip service to werewolf totems (at least when relatives are around). She\u2019s friendly until given a reason to be otherwise. The treatment she\u2019s received from elder werewolves has nearly soured her on filial respect, and it will take serious convincing on the part of any pack to change her mind.&quot;<br /> <br /> So that's the W20 idea of what a loyal shamanistic kin-mage looks like. The elders don't trust her, extremists probably want her dead, and she's basically only helping the Garou because it's better than warring with them after all the crap they've given her. Being a shaman and kin has been such a pain that even packs that don't give a shit about the elders going on about Name-breakers, aren't going to be trusted by her without significant effort of earning it first. And that's what M20 presents as the &quot;best case&quot; magic user scenario. It only gets worse for kinfolk magic users (or magic users in general) from this. Oh, and that sample shaman kinfolk is an Uktena kin; the Tribe that's consistently presented as the most tolerant of magic users among their kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But (especially from a WtA perspective) no Mage would actually do that. </div> </div> </div>That's treating OOC knowledge as IC knowledge. The Garou have no idea how hard it would be for a magic user to twist the minds of the local spirits into thinking the magic-user is super awesome, so the Garou have no reason to assume that a magic user that deals with spirits a lot hasn't at least tried to force a positive impression like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T01:38:49-08:00","id":764778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764672#post764672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did... you read my post? Or just quote a part and ignore the following bit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it. I didn't ignore the following bit, but I quoted the part I wanted to respond to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is nice, but ignoring the point. If a Garou discovers a kinfolk turned vampire using various sensory Gifts, the vast majority of Garou are going to kill the kinfolk-vampire. Not because they're treating Sense Wyrm as dectect evil. But because they consider being a vampire being worse than dead, and once they find out a kin is a vampire they're going to kill it.<br /> <br /> The Garou response to human magic isn't as extreme, but it falls into the same general issue. Finding out a kinfolk is using human magic is already putting that kinfolk into the &quot;shit list&quot; pile. Not because Sense Magic is detect Name Breaker, but because it doesn't take a lot of investigation to say, &quot;Hey what's this magic smell you've got on you? Wait, you're resorting to human magic? WTF!?!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Your previous post sure sounded like it went beyond WTF and straight into murder. Also, the comparison to vampires is not really very helpful.<br /> <br /> After seeing the extremes people bring up in this thread I need to go back and reread Unsung Heroes. Maybe it's just normal for Garou to abusively control their kinfolk like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to derail the thread with silly badwrongfun accusations and snide comments, that's your choice. </div> </div> </div>I am not accusing you of badwrongfun. I am saying that playing Garou like homicidal maniacs, whether as PCs or NPCs, is sort of missing the point. One would think they'd try to rise above their flaws, <i>especially</i> when dealing with kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-13-2015, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T02:00:06-08:00","id":764784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764340#post764340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they're culturally taught not to trust humanity, let alone human magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? 1st Edition Fianna hat mentioned Verbena amongst their kin. In any case, it wouldn't make any sense to believe garou to be totally anti-human-magic if their kin can use it and such use is tolerated. Most TBs also have a general warning about mages, but no outright kill-command.<br /> In any case, if a Sorcerer works shamanistic, the power actually comes from the spirits and these are allowed to use magic and it is fine with the garou. It's not forsaken, right?<br /> So, there is a mechanical difference between a Sorcerer and a human with multiple &quot;Spirit Alley&quot; merits (or one spirit with 'Alter reality' like charms), but thematically they might appear to be the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764340#post764340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, frankly, WtA is full of the Garou being idiots by trusting their gut instincts instead of developing deeper understandings.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have traits for &quot;gut feelings&quot; its Primal-Urge and for deeper understanding, it is Gnosis. But why should the garou be idiots when doing what they feel is right?<br /> They are designed that way - it is Gaia's or God's will.<br /> Being a usually indiscrimination force against human-magic is their place in the universe and necessary to maintain balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T02:27:01-08:00","id":764793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764746#post764746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll quote W20:<br /> <br /> [snip for brevity]<br /> <br /> So that's the W20 idea of what a loyal shamanistic kin-mage looks like. The elders don't trust her, extremists probably want her dead, and she's basically only helping the Garou because it's better than warring with them after all the crap they've given her. Being a shaman and kin has been such a pain that even packs that don't give a shit about the elders going on about Name-breakers, aren't going to be trusted by her without significant effort of earning it first. And that's what M20 presents as the &quot;best case&quot; magic user scenario. It only gets worse for kinfolk magic users (or magic users in general) from this. Oh, and that sample shaman kinfolk is an Uktena kin; the Tribe that's consistently presented as the most tolerant of magic users among their kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is though, W20 also says this, 2nd column, pg 387;<br /> <br /> &quot;While the exact manifestation of these abilities may vary, Kinfolk with their own form of magick may be seen as a strong asset to their Garou family - assuming of course that the Kin has not been alienated by oppression or abuse before their supernatural powers manifested.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not a cut and dry matter whether a magic-wielding kin is going to be accepted or not, it's not even a tribe-by-tribe thing, it's probably closer to a sept-by-sept thing. Some werewolves are going to be sticks in the mud and decry all mortal magics as namebreaking, others will just see another tool to help them in their fight. Kin are by definition family, and family tends to get the benefit of the doubt more than outsiders. Even a stuffy Garou might have opinions on par with &quot;oh sure, <i>THAT </i>namebreaker is a vile tool of the weaver wielding powers beyond his comprehension or wisdom to control, but my cousin Larry who can speak with spirits and brew potions, well <i>HE's</i> alright, he helped me move last spring.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think probably the takeaway is that kinfolk sorcery is exactly as common as you want it to be, kin sorcerers do exist canonically and there isn't a complete consensus among the Garou as to how to deal with them beyond cautious suspicion until they demonstrate that they don't want to raise caerns for their power to fuel their unholy namebreaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T02:54:24-08:00","id":764803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764778#post764778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read it. I didn't ignore the following bit, but I quoted the part I wanted to respond to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really convinced of that. At the moment, it feels like if I don't say, &quot;The Garou don't kill mages on sight!&quot; every other sentence, you're going to treat my posts as just saying, &quot;The Garou will happily kill every kin in the city if the think one might use magic!&quot; because that's what you seem to be getting no matter what I actually said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your previous post sure sounded like it went beyond WTF and straight into murder. Also, the comparison to vampires is not really very helpful. </div> </div> </div>Which part, exactly, went strait to murder?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After seeing the extremes people bring up in this thread I need to go back and reread Unsung Heroes. Maybe it's just normal for Garou to abusively control their kinfolk like this. </div> </div> </div>Sure. Unsung Heroes has it cost 4 freebies to be a tolerated dynamic mage, and 7 freebies to have any Garou actually like you. That's how much weight it puts on the default state being, &quot;the Garou don't like these people.&quot; It's not entirely clear as to whether or not linear mages are meant to buy this (though is probably is supposed to depend on what kind of linear they are).<br /> <br /> And Unsung Heroes is pretty clear that too many of the Garou treating the kin like shit (not even getting into the ones with actual powers) is a long standing problem; esp. as it is seen as lawful behavior (though lots would point out stupid and unproductive). It also points out that plenty of Garou are abusive in the other direction of being massively overprotective, and in the end just as controlling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not accusing you of badwrongfun. </div> </div> </div>Well, you basically did, even if it wasn't your intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am saying that playing Garou like homicidal maniacs, whether as PCs or NPCs, is sort of missing the point. One would think they'd try to rise above their flaws, <i>especially</i> when dealing with kinfolk. </div> </div> </div>First off, keep in mind that the Garou are, objectively, homicidal religious fanatics. They kill people, without any sort of justice system all the time on the sole basis of their religion telling them to. This is the WOD, and the protagonists might be heroes in their own eyes, but that doesn't mean they're not out doing things we'd perceive as bad, or outright evil, if we were on the receiving end o fit.<br /> <br /> And the problem with your thinking, is that you're assuming that the flaws we see, being outside observers to their universe, are things they acknowledge as flaws. You can't rise above a flaw you don't acknowledge is a flaw. The Garou, as a whole, don't see treating the kinfolk as third-class citizens as a flaw. They don't see treating any other supernatural as inherently unworthy of trust until repeatedly proven otherwise a flaw. Some do, but they're the minority, and in thousands of years, there's been little success in shifting the Garou's general disposition on these topics.<br /> <br /> Basically, you're missing the point that your assumptions are based in the Garou reading the gaming books we're talking about, rather than basing your assumptions on what the books say about the Garou's actual view points on these things are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764784#post764784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'm aware there's edition drift out there. But 2e, Rev., and W20 are all fairly consistent on this particular subject. Whipping out some 1e bits really doesn't help anything much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, it wouldn't make any sense to believe garou to be totally anti-human-magic if their kin can use it and such use is tolerated. Most TBs also have a general warning about mages, but no outright kill-command. </div> </div> </div>I quoted W20 above on the default view on magic. I'm not sure how that's unclear. The Garou don't like human magic. They don't like Metis either. Some of them are draconian about these sorts of things, others are more pragmatic.<br /> <br /> And please, quote me saying, once, in this entire thread:<br /> <br /> 1) Saying that the Garou tolerate no human magic ever.<br /> 2) Saying that the Garou kill magic users on sight.<br /> <br /> Because it would be really nice to talk about what I've said, not what I didn't say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, if a Sorcerer works shamanistic, the power actually comes from the spirits and these are allowed to use magic and it is fine with the garou. It's not forsaken, right? </div> </div> </div>Sigh.<br /> <br /> Can we please stop trying to make this black &amp; white nonsense? There is space between, &quot;The Garou are fine with it,&quot; and, &quot;it is completely forsaken.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, I quoted from the W20 core book above, about a shaman character and how she's treated by the Garou. No, being a shaman isn't enough to get an automatic pass from the Garou according to the books; drawing power from the spirits isn't something that kinfolk are supposed to be doing. It's just better than being some other kind of magic user (keeping in mind that the Garou have no real way to tell the difference between mages and sorcerers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, there is a mechanical difference between a Sorcerer and a human with multiple &quot;Spirit Alley&quot; merits (or one spirit with 'Alter reality' like charms), but thematically they might appear to be the same. </div> </div> </div>Those mechanical differences matter to how the Garou will react though. They can tell the difference (with the right powers anyway) between a kinfolk that's got a spirit blessing their lives, and a kinfolk that's used magic of some sort to draw a spirits power into them. Even if it looks very similar to casual perusal, once it gets their attention, they'd be able to tell the difference rather quickly assuming any of the Garou around have the abilities to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have traits for &quot;gut feelings&quot; its Primal-Urge and for deeper understanding, it is Gnosis. But why should the garou be idiots when doing what they feel is right? </div> </div> </div>Gnosis... isn't about a deeper understanding of everything.<br /> <br /> And the Garou do stupid things because they feel a constant pressure to act, thus denying them time to adequately think things through and gather evidence. That's a recipe for repeatedly doing the wrong thing because it felt right at the time. Also, the Garou have Rage, which means they have a fairly regular part of them that &quot;feels right&quot; in ripping things to shreds that they need to restrain because it's often not the best idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T02:57:41-08:00","id":764805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764793#post764793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a cut and dry matter...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact:<br /> <br /> I never fucking said it was.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T02:59:11-08:00","id":764806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764805#post764805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact:<br /> <br /> I never fucking said it was.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, didn't mean to come across as confrontational.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T03:59:42-08:00","id":764828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764806#post764806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, didn't mean to come across as confrontational.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither did I.<br /> <br /> Regarding the garous' ability to sense and differate magic there are some assumptions in the room, I guess.<br /> 1st - Do gifts like Sense the Unnatural, Sense magic and the like offer a catalogue of types of magic or has a garou to build up their own, meaning that they have to find out, what a certain type of magic &quot;feels like&quot; and then how it is called? And can they convey the type they sensed after the fact? Meaning, can an Uktena tell another, I felt &quot;this-and-that&quot; and another states, &quot;ah, that's human sorcery&quot; or would they both have to be at the scene and use the gift and then teach &quot;That, young padawan, is human sorcery&quot;.<br /> <br /> Spinning out from this, you have to re-evaluate the status quo. If every garou would have to learn what this and that is to make an educated statement for every single type of encounter they have with magic. And all other garou would have to fall back on speculation.<br /> <br /> Also, what makes &quot;human magic&quot; human?<br /> If sorcery is bad, and true magic is bad, what is wrong with cantips, that they aren't ? Changelings are essentially humans, kinain even more so. And psionics, are they magic human or another breed entirely. Human-form Kami, and other possessed (well, most are bad because of what they do) ?<br /> Mummies are often allied with garou, Gypsies ?<br /> <br /> Without a successful roll on &quot;Scent the true form&quot; most garou can't even tell the difference. So, while garou would not like magic amongst humans in general, they in every actual case still have to evaluate what is going on and who to react.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T04:09:22-08:00","id":764832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764778#post764778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your previous post sure sounded like it went beyond WTF and straight into murder. Also, the comparison to vampires is not really very helpful.<br /> <br /> After seeing the extremes people bring up in this thread I need to go back and reread Unsung Heroes. Maybe it's just normal for Garou to abusively control their kinfolk like this.<br /> <br /> I am not accusing you of badwrongfun. I am saying that playing Garou like homicidal maniacs, whether as PCs or NPCs, is sort of missing the point. One would think they'd try to rise above their flaws, <i>especially</i> when dealing with kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> You expect too much. In another WtA thread it was explained to me in great detail, why we &quot;clueless&quot; VtM players suck, that Werewolves always win against Vampires, sense things on chance encounters when even all WtA rulebooks deny it and that any kind of idea to not slay Vampires, Mages, other factions on sight is incompatible with WtA lore. And therefore I should better pack off back to love, peace and harmony Masquerade.<br /> In this forum is a rather hardcore faction of WtA players, one I never encountered before. I simply raised the question why the Werewolves never try a different solution from killing others without even thinking, when the Garou know(!) that their usual tactics fail more and more. That one should think about temporary cease-fires with their &quot;lesser&quot; enemies to win over common enemies of both. But I was directly derided as a peace-lover, know-nothing, since all cease-fires with enemy factions were supposdly broken by said enemies. Considering the typical behaviour of Garou I am sure that is Garou propaganda and one of these omnicidal maniacs snapped and broke the cease-fire before the Vampire, Mages or whoever did.<br /> &quot;Fur and Claws for the win, thinking is overestimated&quot; seems to be the motto for a faction here. Which is sad, as you wrote, since WtA is about more than hack and slay.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T04:19:12-08:00","id":764838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764803#post764803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you basically did, even if it wasn't your intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I am sorry. Consider it retracted.<br /> <br /> I don't have anything to add to the rest of your post, which I <i>did</i> read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T07:31:30-08:00","id":764917,"title":"","content":"The whole thing is a non-issue most of the time thanks to the fact that Sorcerors are quite rare and need to find a source that will teach them. Since kinfolk tend to hang with their own, their exposure to groups that could teach them is quite rare. Worse yet, most of the printed Paths are quite dubious as picks and as something for the Garou to digest.<br /> <br /> However, I've always had the opinion that the most common and acceptable Path among the Kinfolk is the one of Enchantment (that's the crafting one, right?) - to the point that I actually used them as a npc support group for crafters and mystics. Mind you, I do not use Mage terms or contrivances - they are simply a group of kinfolk dedicated to crafting and using ancestral techniques given from father to son for the past thousands of years. Their style is deeply influenced and patterned on the practices of the Theurges.<br /> <br /> The Path of Enchantment allows for specialised skills and knowledges that are perfect for the craftsman, since actually making weapons of silver and all the goods that will pass the muster in the eyes of a spirit is a great endeavour, as i deeply doubt that most Theurges are masters of both the spirits and craftsmanships.<br /> <br /> The other form of Kinfolk magic that i use is giving them low level rituals and gifts. A lot can be achieved with them, allowing you to fulfil most narrative roles you could need from them. This is something that works within the confines of Werewolf and that is supported by the setting.<br /> <br /> Classic sorcery and true magic brings with it way too much baggage. The former is pretty much married to a long standing organisation and mentors who would intrude into the Kinfolk's lives enough to be a threat to the Garou, and the latter makes a disservice for the Mage to be in service of the Garou and their goals rather then themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T10:53:15-08:00","id":765042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764828#post764828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st - Do gifts like Sense the Unnatural, Sense magic and the like offer a catalogue of types of magic or has a garou to build up their own, meaning that they have to find out, what a certain type of magic &quot;feels like&quot; and then how it is called? And can they convey the type they sensed after the fact? Meaning, can an Uktena tell another, I felt &quot;this-and-that&quot; and another states, &quot;ah, that's human sorcery&quot; or would they both have to be at the scene and use the gift and then teach &quot;That, young padawan, is human sorcery&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending a bit on the Gift and the successes rolled:<br /> <br /> 1) The level of detailed offered is left at the supernatural &quot;type&quot; level. A vampire or blood magics are detected differently from a wraith and Arcanoi, and so on. The books leave mages and sorcerers in something of a undifferentiated state without ever clearly addressing how to separate a Hermetic dynamic mage from a Hermetic linear mage. Most of these Gifts directly identify the thing in question though. Scent of the True Form says, &quot;that's a leech, that's a wizard, that's a fae.&quot; without prerequisite knowledge of those groups specific natures.<br /> <br /> 2) Sense Magic of the baseline Gifts for this is only one that seems to convey this sort of information in a way that could be taught outside of knowing the Gift, since it operates more like Auspex 2 or other aura scanning powers (though it isn't dealing with auras) in terms of delivery a suite of sensory information that indicates specific aspects of the magic in question. The text leaves enough leeway that particularly rare kinds of magic could lead to the user not being sure what they sensed, and thus to a more experienced Garou informing them that the feeling they had means X; but that seems to mostly be for things like Mummies or Kuei-jin that Western Garou never really see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what makes &quot;human magic&quot; human? </div> </div> </div>From a Garou's perspective? It doesn't come from spirits/Gnosis/ghosts, vampires, fae, or other lesser known but clearly inhuman (from a Garou point of view) entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings are essentially humans, kinain even more so. And psionics, are they magic human or another breed entirely. Human-form Kami, and other possessed (well, most are bad because of what they do) ?<br /> Mummies are often allied with garou, Gypsies ? </div> </div> </div>The fae aren't tolerated well by the Garou either (though like the Uktena are more tolerant of magic users, the Fianna are more tolerant of the fae). Kin fae face the same 4/7 freebie issue to be tolerated/have anyone actually like them. The fae are taught too be to unstable to trust and form full alliances with.<br /> <br /> Psychics are numina users, just like hedge wizards and true faith weilders.<br /> <br /> Kami are more like kinfolk with Gnosis. They're blessed directly by Gaia, and some Garou might not like that, but aren't going to argue with their primary goddess on it either.<br /> <br /> Pre-Revised mummies are presented as too rare and too reclusive to have any solid stereotypes about. It's hinted that the Garou can easily mistake them for things they like less due to that unfamiliarity but hard to say more. Post-Revised mummies are really only allied with the Silent Striders against their mutual enemies; this new breed of mummy is too new to know how things would play out in the long term for Garou/Mummy relations.<br /> <br /> And... lets not touch WOD: Gypsies? Ok?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764917#post764917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I've always had the opinion that the most common and acceptable Path among the Kinfolk is the one of Enchantment (that's the crafting one, right?) - to the point that I actually used them as a npc support group for crafters and mystics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemy (crafting of a different sort), Healing, and Spirit Chasing (since it was presented as a Kinfolk path in Unsung Heroes) are probably also fairly common by these standards and generally far more accepted than things like Hellfire or Summoning/Warding/Binding would be.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T10:56:54-08:00","id":765046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=765042#post765042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemy (crafting of a different sort), Healing, and Spirit Chasing (since it was presented as a Kinfolk path in Unsung Heroes) are probably also fairly common by these standards and generally far more accepted than things like Hellfire or Summoning/Warding/Binding would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemy and Healing with a strong dose of herbalism and traditional medicine, sure. Again, I would postulate that there are Kinfolk ony magical societies which they are a part of. What does Spirit Chasing do?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T11:35:15-08:00","id":765070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=765046#post765046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alchemy and Healing with a strong dose of herbalism and traditional medicine, sure. Again, I would postulate that there are Kinfolk ony magical societies which they are a part of. What does Spirit Chasing do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically allows a hedge mage to sympathise with a particular form of plant or animal spirit, gaining abilities related to it, like a plant shaman being able to live off sunlight and water or a deer shaman being able to leap extremely high. Like Bravestarr or Animal Man gain animal powers without actually shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T16:44:51-08:00","id":765218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=765046#post765046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alchemy and Healing with a strong dose of herbalism and traditional medicine, sure. Again, I would postulate that there are Kinfolk ony magical societies which they are a part of. What does Spirit Chasing do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll also point out that Ephemera (Spirit Summoning) was listed as a -1 difficulty for Kinfolk a couple of times before it was rolled into Summoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T23:12:45-08:00","id":765375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=764693#post764693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always bin of the mind that sorcery is more then just &amp;quot;here kid read a book, your a wizard now!&amp;quot;. That the individual was born under a sign, right condition or destined somehow to wield the power.<br /> <br /> Granted some old guy who has studied his whole life might know a dot or two in a path but the real deal was destined for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to think of it as something that largely hinges on early development. I have read that the older we get that the harder it becomes to recognize or process different phonemes when learning new languages, and that its primarily children who start young really get the hang of mastering the subtleties of foreign language pronounciation. I suspect that most people could develop a decent talent for sorcery, but only when they can begin at an age where their minds are still able to develop an Awareness or Kenning score and can learn how to attune themselves to otherworldly forces. And even then it takes a good teacher and constant work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T00:09:57-08:00","id":765410,"title":"","content":"The language parallel is a bit more nuanced in a way that I think matters. While it is generally true that most people do better with languages when they're exposed at a younger age, that is more of an &quot;average&quot; than a universal truth. Some people are always going to suck at language acquisition (my sister tested for a learning disability in this, I tested on the edge) even for languages they were raised around. Other people (my brother-in-law's family is full of people like this) has brains that never turn off the early acquisition stuff, and pick up new languages with annoying ease well into old age.<br /> <br /> Magical aptitude should probably be seen the same way. Some people are just never really going to have the talent. Some people might get the talent if they're raised in the right environment, and others are just naturals with it who will pick it up whenever they finally get exposed to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T03:42:23-08:00","id":766161,"title":"","content":"The write up for 'Kin/Mage' also had a lot of political and cultural baggage, with not only divided loyalties, but also an incompatible religion with her tribe.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think that most with magical abilities are going to divide their loyalties like that. They'll either stick with family &amp; the cause, or be sick of it and largely nreak away. (Kinda sounded like what the write up was doing.)<br /> <br /> I also don't think any large Societies are going to be well received, and I figure that those that exist would be rather covert .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T05:22:56-08:00","id":775401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=765042#post765042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a Garou's perspective? It doesn't come from spirits/Gnosis/ghosts, vampires, fae, or other lesser known but clearly inhuman (from a Garou point of view) entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the gift does that. I mean, if I wanted to build a shaman, who had powers granted by the spirits I would use Sorcerer rules to build such a character. The Sorcerer books specifically states, that the method or tradition of the sorcerer can be pretty much anything from a hermetic to a techno-mage - so shaman would be within the scope.<br /> <br /> The gift allows for the garou to detect the &quot;kind of magic&quot; but not necessarily the source of the magic. Essentially stating, that hedge magic could be a means to appeal to the spirits just as much as a garou rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=765042#post765042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fae aren't tolerated well by the Garou either [....] The fae are taught too be to unstable to trust and form full alliances with.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not that their magic was unnatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=765042#post765042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psychics are numina users, just like hedge wizards and true faith weilders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would gifts make a difference between their powers or not ?<br /> Are all numina the same? I would say no. But I also would say, that all Hedge magic isn't the same either, for sorcerers have to choose means by which they use their powers and that is a differentiating aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=765042#post765042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-Revised mummies are presented as too rare and too reclusive to have any solid stereotypes about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet alliances between mummies, mokol\u00e9 and Silent Striders are depicted as common before the Striders were cursed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; really tell a person &quot;This is a vampire&quot; ?<br /> I never read it that way and it kind of couldn't wrap my head around it, if it did. I mean you smell a &quot;Vrushdack&quot;. You have no idea what a vrushdack is. So, you tell your pack &quot;That smells like a vrushdack&quot;. &quot;A what?&quot; &quot;A vrushdack. I don't know what that is, the name just popped into my mind - by smell&quot;.<br /> <br /> Doesn't make any sense to me. Even less with mokol\u00e9 who have &quot;Sight of the true form&quot;.<br /> Also, if a name popped into your mind - what language would it be...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T05:40:14-08:00","id":775410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=775401#post775401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; really tell a person &quot;This is a vampire&quot; ?<br /> I never read it that way and it kind of couldn't wrap my head around it, if it did. I mean you smell a &quot;Vrushdack&quot;. You have no idea what a vrushdack is. So, you tell your pack &quot;That smells like a vrushdack&quot;. &quot;A what?&quot; &quot;A vrushdack. I don't know what that is, the name just popped into my mind - by smell&quot;.<br /> <br /> Doesn't make any sense to me. Even less with mokol\u00e9 who have &quot;Sight of the true form&quot;.<br /> Also, if a name popped into your mind - what language would it be...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scent of the True Form does tell somewhat what it is, but you have to learn what the smell means when encountering first time:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou can smell Kinfolk or a fellow werewolf automatically. In all other cases, the player must roll Perception + Primal-Urge (difficulty 6). One success will identify a normal human or animal; two successes will detect a vampire, changeling, demon, mummy, or Fera; four successes are needed to sniff out a mage, ghoul, or fomor. The Imbued register as normal humans to this Gift. Unfamiliar scents aren\u2019t automatically recognized:... </div> </div> </div>But Sense Wyrm tells &quot;<b>WYRM!</b>&quot; in loud, bold letters, once humanity of a Vampire is on the dwinding road....<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires register as Wyrm-tainted, save those with Humanity ratings of 7 or higher. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T07:46:54-08:00","id":775464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=775401#post775401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how the gift does that. I mean, if I wanted to build a shaman, who had powers granted by the spirits I would use Sorcerer rules to build such a character. The Sorcerer books specifically states, that the method or tradition of the sorcerer can be pretty much anything from a hermetic to a techno-mage - so shaman would be within the scope.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gift doesn't say that it can tell the difference between a Hermetic using Binding to &quot;force&quot; a spirit to do something, or a shaman using Binding after careful negotiations.<br /> <br /> It would just sense that a Spirit is bound with human magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Essentially stating, that hedge magic could be a means to appeal to the spirits just as much as a garou rite. </div> </div> </div>Except that the Garou are universally taught (even the Uktena) that this isn't the case. Some human magic users are <i>bether</i> than others because they at least are trying to be respectful of the spirits, but that doesn't mean their magics are every going to be sense as the ethical equals of a Garou rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But not that their magic was unnatural. </div> </div> </div>By definition, the Garou concept of &quot;unnatural&quot; includes them. That doens't mean they're right (though Gifts like &quot;Sense the Unnatural&quot; do operate that Fae are in the same sensory category as vampires), it just means they're biased as hell against anything that doesn't operate according to their conceptualization of how the world is supposed to work.<br /> <br /> You seem to be taking far too much of a, &quot;OOC I know everything because I read the books,&quot; stance on this, rather than what the Garou would know from their teachings, and what their powers allow them to sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are all numina the same? I would say no. But I also would say, that all Hedge magic isn't the same either, for sorcerers have to choose means by which they use their powers and that is a differentiating aspect. </div> </div> </div>Quote me a passage in the relevant Gifts that backs this up. I've more than done my share of citing the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yet alliances between mummies, mokol\u00e9 and Silent Striders are depicted as common before the Striders were cursed. </div> </div> </div>And... just like the Fae, and magic users, there's one Tribe that has more dealings with some other supernaturals than normal. And the books vary greatly on how &quot;common &quot; that was between editions. It's also fairly moot since there's no Striders left from those times and Striders don't get Ancestors to channel for past-life info on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; really tell a person &quot;This is a vampire&quot; ? </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, got beaten to the specifics.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T10:43:09-08:00","id":775545,"title":"","content":"In fact the Silent Strider/Mummy alliance thing was listed as strained and that was in the second edition book. <br /> As for the various Sense gifts vampires are not alive they are magically animated corpses even the most humane vampire will smell of clotted/old blood.<br /> Mages depending on belief might smell weaverish all of the Science mages, Hermetic houses, etc. Some may smell slightly wyrmish Euthantos, Verbena, possibly Dreamspeakers, and of course Nephandi as for telling what a Mage is they more than likely crackle with power and smell of ozone.<br /> Fae probably shimmer as they switch back and forth between their fae seeming and human appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T05:51:57-08:00","id":777700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=775464#post775464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gift doesn't say that it can tell the difference between a Hermetic using Binding to &quot;force&quot; a spirit to do something, or a shaman using Binding after careful negotiations.<br /> <br /> It would just sense that a Spirit is bound with human magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedge magic that is, even when performed by a Uktena, Bastet or whatever...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=775464#post775464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be taking far too much of a, &quot;OOC I know everything because I read the books,&quot; stance on this, rather than what the Garou would know from their teachings, and what their powers allow them to sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having played LARP a lot and seen plenty of players starting as cubs with no idea and running in this very problem. They don't know anything OOC but they still don't believe what the player's who play older characters tell them to be right.<br /> <br /> For me that always raises the logical question. If gifts can't divine it and there is no other definitive reason to think human magic is wrong, then why do all garou think it?<br /> Sure some might have had bad experiences and therefore influences a prejudice to believe so. But that would be local and other experiences by other garou would contradict this, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> I just find it hard to believe and see how other players have a hard time to convey it to newbies, it a certain believe is not in the Setting. If all Hedge magic would come at a cost, like all magic in &quot;Once upon a time&quot; does, leaching life forces, slowly feeding banes of power and such - then I would get why garou oppose it vehemently. But stating that it is unnatural, when actually people could fo it for ages, when actually the diversion of matter and spirit that is unnatural is the reason that there isn't magic in our everyday life, seems just as an unfounded stance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=775464#post775464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quote me a passage in the relevant Gifts that backs this up. I've more than done my share of citing the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have the books with me, so googled to Wyrmfoe.com. There sense magic states &quot;The difficulty is based on the strength and subtlety of the magic. The Uktena cannot tell the exact nature of the magic, although vague clues such as \u201cGaian\u201d or \u201cblood magic\u201d might be granted with sufficient successes. The radius is 10 feet per success.&quot;<br /> Sense the Unnatural states &quot;The sensory input is somewhat vague and subject to interpretation though. For instance, a vampire might smell of old blood, of fear, of rotten flesh, of fresh meat or of whatever else the Storyteller finds appropriate. Interpreting the information properly might require an Intelligence + Occult roll (Storyteller\u2019s option).&quot;<br /> <br /> So, I read that like a &quot;cult of ecstasy&quot;-like witch, a druid-own-blood-sacrificer, a voodoo-inspired necromancer and a gadget-wielding technomancer all get very different descriptions, in varying details depending on successes - despite all being hedge magic users on a rules level.<br /> <br /> So, to some degree I think my view is a lot more In-Character - judging the setting by what experiences the garou might have had in the past - as opposed on the fact that it all is a specific numina that handles the mechanics.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;Scent of the true form&quot;. The quote would continue &quot;Unfamiliar scents aren't automatically recognized: A Philodox that has never encountered any Rokea might not immediately recognize the scent she detects as &quot;wereshark.&quot;<br /> So, no the gift does not grant the information &quot;This is a vampire&quot; it grants the information &quot;this is something like you never used this gift on before&quot; (or never smelled before, if what you smell when not using/before learning the gift is also considered to be a known smell). If the same is true for magic, garou would have a harder time finding out about human magic, for they too would just encounter something &quot;not encountered before&quot; and than would have to investigate who the originator was. But as stated above, the magic sensing gifts allow for more information per successes - albeit I don't see that they discern by game mechanics but should discern by in-game aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T02:41:09-08:00","id":778209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=777700#post777700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me that always raises the logical question. If gifts can't divine it and there is no other definitive reason to think human magic is wrong, then why do all garou think it?<br /> Sure some might have had bad experiences and therefore influences a prejudice to believe so. But that would be local and other experiences by other garou would contradict this, wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the reason for some of the Wars of Rage? I think it was something akin to the following list... &quot;They fly and drink blood! Kill the Bats!&quot; &quot;They don't give us the gift of revival! Kill the Bears!&quot; &quot;They don't tell us their secrets! Kill the Cats!&quot; &quot;They don't look like Wolves! Kill the Bunyip!&quot;<br /> <br /> That looks pretty much like Garou hate Hedge magic because they can't learn it usually - and because the common Witchhunter wields it and hunts Werewolfs with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=777700#post777700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just find it hard to believe and see how other players have a hard time to convey it to newbies, it a certain believe is not in the Setting. If all Hedge magic would come at a cost, like all magic in &quot;Once upon a time&quot; does, leaching life forces, slowly feeding banes of power and such - then I would get why garou oppose it vehemently. But stating that it is unnatural, when actually people could fo it for ages, when actually the diversion of matter and spirit that is unnatural is the reason that there isn't magic in our everyday life, seems just as an unfounded stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedge Magic is (IIRC) done by pure Willpower &amp; some ritual most times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=777700#post777700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't have the books with me, so googled to Wyrmfoe.com. There sense magic states &quot;The difficulty is based on the strength and subtlety of the magic. The Uktena cannot tell the exact nature of the magic, although vague clues such as \u201cGaian\u201d or \u201cblood magic\u201d might be granted with sufficient successes. The radius is 10 feet per success.&quot;<br /> Sense the Unnatural states &quot;The sensory input is somewhat vague and subject to interpretation though. For instance, a vampire might smell of old blood, of fear, of rotten flesh, of fresh meat or of whatever else the Storyteller finds appropriate. Interpreting the information properly might require an Intelligence + Occult roll (Storyteller\u2019s option).&quot;<br /> <br /> So, I read that like a &quot;cult of ecstasy&quot;-like witch, a druid-own-blood-sacrificer, a voodoo-inspired necromancer and a gadget-wielding technomancer all get very different descriptions, in varying details depending on successes - despite all being hedge magic users on a rules level.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Rite changes the tingle? Possible, but maybe the personal taint also marks it. If two people perfoprm the exact same rite, both have a slightly different &quot;vibe&quot;, resulting in being able to pick out who did it with (5+?) successes on the discerning or that extra interpretation roll?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T02:50:00-08:00","id":778211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=778209#post778209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the reason for some of the Wars of Rage? I think it was something akin to the following list... &quot;They fly and drink blood! Kill the Bats!&quot; &quot;They don't give us the gift of revival! Kill the Bears!&quot; &quot;They don't tell us their secrets! Kill the Cats!&quot; &quot;They don't look like Wolves! Kill the Bunyip!&quot;<br /> <br /> That looks pretty much like Garou hate Hedge magic because they can't learn it usually - and because the common Witchhunter wields it and hunts Werewolfs with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou can learn Hedge Magic, just like all the other shapeshifters. It's just that they don't usually bother as Rites and Gifts are vastly superior.<br /> <br /> As for the War(s) of Rage... It's way more complex than that. Garou can be assholes, but they are not utter idiots. There were quite a few things going wrong, there were a number of manipulations by the Wyrm involved, and there was a a lot of pride among all the sides involved that turned shows of force into all out bloodbaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T03:39:24-08:00","id":778229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hira Akigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=778209#post778209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge Magic is (IIRC) done by pure Willpower &amp; some ritual most times.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a mechanical standpoint, sure. But in-character they have different methods or tools they need. Being hermetics, shamans, druids, herbalists, making use of angelic symbols, cabbalistic tradition, far east mysticism and so on.<br /> All of these methods grant hedge magic and unlike shadowrun they do not come with limits or additional benefits to the hedge magic paths one can learn. But iirc the Sorcerer revised character creation wants you to pick at least one such method or tool. And it is what lets you do magic (despite your will, training, and the fact that you bought the numina trait)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:38:18-08:00","id":778678,"title":"","content":"The first and primary answer:<br /> <br /> It's as common as you nee\u200bd it for the story you are trying to tell.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:55:39-08:00","id":780787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761273#post761273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that there's probably a greater percentage of sorcerers among the kinfolk than there is among the general human population, just because at least some of them are raised in a culture where magic and the spirit world is objectively known to exist. Definitely among the Uktena they'd probably be even relatively common, maybe as much as one or more per kin community. Some Garou might not want their kin practicing magic or having any real power though, especially in the wake of the Sam Haight incident - clear proof for the conservative side that kin knowing rites and genuine occult lore is a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, none of what Samuel learned was through other garou or kinfolk, so it's a pretty shaky argument. But who ever said conservatives were really worried about being logic or sensible? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761897#post761897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree completely. The amount of justification to have such knowledge is often overlooked because mechanics-wise, you just buy it with XP. In &quot;reality&quot; though, you have to devoted your life to mastering such esoteric knowledge. Any form of magic is a kind of spiritual discipline, but that doesn't show up when it comes to acquiring it in game.<br /> <br /> I would not be surprised if at various times, a secret lodge among the kinfolk arose that had knowledge of hedge magic. However, the Garou are jealous of their status as Gaia's defenders, and if they find out about it - which they eventually will - things will not turn out well for those kinfolk hedge wizards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the tribe and local culture of specific septs and communities i guess - doling out fragments of such lore in layers through mystery cults would be pretty consistent with their cultural and mythic roots. Bone Gnawers are kind of &quot;whatever works as long as you don't stink of Wyrm&quot;. The norse culture the Get harken back to has strong traditions of magic, not to mention that kinfolk actually initiated in such lore could be of great help in containing the plague of debased wyrm-touched magic under the guise of Asatru that has spread through a number of &quot;spiritually-minded&quot; neo-nazi groups and such, a sore spot of the tribe. Shadow Lords might accept kinfolk empowerment based on their own principles of survival of the strongest/most cunning and so on. Tribal leaders are individuals, each with their own particular take of their people's traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/761192-how-common-should-hedge-magic-be-among-kinfolk?p=761897#post761897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players often have a &quot;we're in this all together&quot; so it's great for the Garou if their kinfolk are mages, hedge wizards, or whatever. This is a very naive view of how protective of their turf people are, and how much infighting occurs within organizations.<br /> <br /> Even if some kinfolk only had access to Ephemera - which is justifiable based on the kinfolk base of knowledge - I don't think the Garou would be supportive of it. The kinfolk are usurping the role of the Garou and being uppity. If such things exist, it's probably very limited - with specific paths being available within specific sects/traditions of specific tribes, and being overseen/approved by elder Garou to make sure such magic if done &quot;properly&quot; and controlled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usurping or supporting? Even a competent sorcerer would have some problem &quot;going to the trenches&quot; where the weird things are, be it the near Umbra or a skyscraper downtown in the wee hours of night. Garou have a bunch of advantages in dealing with spirits &amp; stuff over kinfolk, empowered or not. But a kinfolk that does some weird tricks can be less of a innocent bystander or defenseless target against the enemies of the Garou Nation. They can be a decent support or warning system, indirecting expanding the range of their Garou relatives and covering up usually vulnerable spots. Some soldiers try to make the most of every soldier or tool can get their hands into. The pride and traditionalism of one is the insecure bellyaching of another. And these differences can generate strife, that makes for great dramatic fodder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-05-2015, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T05:41:29-07:00","id":878677,"title":"","content":"&quot;Bless me Father for I have Sinned I have commited the Mortal sin of Thread Necromancy&quot;<br /> <br /> Something I wanted to ask, about how gifts and numina interact... Thinking in particular can a Kin with the &quot;Astral projection&quot; Numina use gifts like &quot;Echoes&quot; or &quot;heightened senses&quot; While projected.<br /> <br /> It could be argued That sense gifts are spiritual in nature the answer should be yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:04:00-07:00","id":878951,"title":"","content":"Given the two systems aren't really meant to interact, there's rarely an official answer. It's mostly going to be, &quot;use your judgement based on what the Numina says it does, and what the Gift says it does.&quot;<br /> <br /> Though having a kin that has Numina, Gnosis, and Gifts is insanely special enough there's a reason this doesn't really get covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:07:25-07:00","id":878954,"title":"","content":"heightened senses and echoes, neither of them call for gnosis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><